[[ ## reasoning ## ]] 
To create the desired bar chart, we need to transform the provided data to extract the project.startDate and project.status fields. Since the data contains nested objects and arrays, we'll use Vega-Lite's 'flatten' transform to access these fields. We'll also use the 'fold' transform to create separate rows for each project status. The x-axis will represent the project.startDate, and the y-axis will represent the count of projects for each status. The bars will be colored by the position of the employee.

[[ ## vega_spec ## ]]
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "data": {
    "values": []
  },
  "transform": [
    {
      "flatten": ["employee.projects"],
      "as": ["project"]
    },
    {
      "fold": ["project.status"],
      "as": ["status", "value"]
    }
  ],
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "project.startDate",
      "type": "temporal"
    },
    "y": {
      "aggregate": "count",
      "type": "quantitative"
    },
    "color": {
      "field": "employee.position",
      "type": "nominal"
    }
  }
}
```
